    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> Muslim state ruled by the Garen lineage, which claimed holy Arab descent, in the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shebelle-river">Shabelle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jubba-river">Jubba</a> rivers.</li><li>Its power rested on control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> and river water, which it used to levy tribute from herders and farmers.</li><li>Revolts in the late 17th century broke it up, and the Hiraab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a> and the Geledi took over its lands.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Many old stone-lined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> across southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> are still attributed by local tradition to the Ajuran, centuries after the sultanate disappeared.</p></aside>
    </section>

